Material Characterization: The crystal phase of as-synthesized samples was determined via XRD measurements using an X'Pert Pro diffractometer. Raman spectroscopy measurements were conducted using a Lab RAM Aramis micro-Raman spectrometer. The morphology of the samples was observed on a Hitachi SU8000 scanning electron microscope. TEM and EDX mapping images were obtained on a JEM2100 transmission electron microscope, and HAADF-STEM images were obtained on the FEI Titan Cubed Themis G2 300 scanning transmission electron microscope. XPS dates were obtained on a K-Alpha X-ray photoelectron spectrometer (Thermo Fisher Scientific). The X-ray absorption experiments were carried out at the XAS station (BL14W1) of the Shanghai Synchrotron Radiation Facility (SSRF). The pore properties and specific surface areas of the samples were derived from ${\sf N}_{2}$ adsorption–desorption isotherm measurement on a Micromeritics ASAP 2010 micropore size analyzer. The metal contents in as-synthesized samples were determined by inductively coupled plasma-optical emission spectrometry (ICP-OES) on PerkinElmer Optima 7000DV analyzer. The conductivities of the samples were assessed using an X3 Hall Effect Test System (Semishare International Limited). The detailed instrument procedures are provided in the Supporting Information.
Electromagnetic Parameter Measurements: The electromagnetic parameters of the samples were measured using a vector network analyzer (Anritsu MS4644A Vectorstar) in the range of $2-78{\mathsf{G H z}}$ . The mixtures (mixed absorbing materials with paraffin matrix) were pressed into toroidal-shaped specimens (the outer diameter of $7.00\ m\ m$ , the inner diameter of $3.04~\mathsf{m m}$ , and the height of ${\approx}3.00~\mathsf{m m}$ ).
## 4. Experimental Section
Chemicals: Hydrous n-hexane and N, N-dimethylformamide were provided by Sinopharm Chemical Reagent Co., Ltd. (China). 2-aminoterephthalic acid $(\geq98.0\%)$ , aluminum chloride hexahydrate $(A l C l_{3}\cdot6H_{2}O$ , $298.0\%$ , nickel chloride $(\mathsf{N i C l}_{2}\cdot6\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O})$ , dicyandiamide, and aqueous hydrofluoric acid $(40\mathrm{~wt.\%})$ were purchased from Shanghai Macklin Biochemical Co., Ltd. (China). All chemicals were used as received without further purification.
Preparation of NiDCD@MIL-101- $N H_{2};$ $M|L-707-N H_{2}$ was synthesized according to the method reported.[56] In particular, $500~{\mathsf{m g}}$ of dehydrated $M L-707-N H_{2}$ were suspended in $700m L$ of dry $n$ -hexane as the hydrophobic solvent, and the mixture was sonicated for ${\approx}30$ min until it became homogenous. After stirring for $5\min$ , $0.67~\mathrm{mL}$ of DMF solution containing $\boldsymbol{\mathsf{100}}\mathrm{mg}$ of DCD and $\boldsymbol{100}~\mathrm{mg}$ of $N i C l_{2}\cdot6H_{2}O$ as the hydrophilic solvent were added dropwise during a period of 30 min. The solution was stirred continuously for another $3h$ . After that, the solid obtained from the centrifugation was dried at room temperature in the air. The synthesized sample, labeled as $N i\mathsf{D C D@M l L cdot707{\cdot}N H_{2}}$ , was further dried at $60^{\circ}C$ under vacuum for $24\mathrm{~h~}$ . Two other specimens, in which DCD and $N i C l_{2}\cdot6H_{2}O$ were used individually (labeled $D{\mathsf{C D}}@{\mathsf{M l L}}.707.{\mathsf{N H}}_{2}$ and ${\mathsf{N i}}@{\mathsf{M l L}}{\mathsf{-l07-N H}}_{2}$ respectively) were also prepared following the same synthesis procedures.
